## Workflow Recipes

**"Just give me the requirements, I'll code myself"**
```
/agent-req <ID>
# Review .ai/specs/<id>-*/explain.md, then code manually
```

**"Generate a plan, then execute it"**
```
/agent-req <ID>
/agent-plan
/agent-plan-validate
/agent-step-all
/agent-step-build
/agent-pr
```

**"Step through manually, review each step"**
```
/agent-step        # Execute one step (includes test, review, commit)
# Repeat for each step
```

**"Answer and fix PR review comments"**
```
/agent-pr-answer   # Research + draft answers, apply agree-will-fix changes
```

**"Full requirements pipeline"**
```
/agent-req <ID>                  # Full pipeline: fetch → dor → explain → research → share
```

Each step is idempotent — already-completed steps are skipped. Dependency chain:
```
fetch → dor → explain → research → share
              ↻ BA checkbox loop
```

**"Full pipeline start to finish"**
```
/agent-agent-all <ID>
```

## Cross-Repo Tickets

Some tickets require changes in multiple repos. Run the workflow in each repo independently:

```
# In first repo:
/agent-req <ID>   # research.md lists other repos involved
/agent-plan           # plans only the changes for THIS repo
/agent-step-all

# Switch to second repo, run same workflow
/agent-req <ID>
/agent-plan
/agent-step-all
```

